# What the squid form, booted as it ships, without a shell and without a
# config, must say on its console (make check-shellfree-squid; test/boot;
# forms/demo/test/console has the format). Given no client networks,
# service-config refuses its settings and Squid parks, saying why, before
# squid-setup writes a list or Squid binds :3128. make check-squid boots
# it with its config, and checks what it lets through.

seen    squid-needs-networks  service-config: \{"event":"settings","service":"squid","setting":"networks","why":"required"\}
seen    squid-parked          leash: \{"event":"down","service":"squid","why":"settings refused; service-config said why"\}
unseen  setup-ran             squid-setup: clients from
